hciattach_rome: pass a size_t to getline()

getline() takes 'size_t *' for its second argument, but hciattach_rome.c
declares bytes_read as int. Older compilers only warned; GCC now rejects it:

  tools/hciattach_rome.c:846:31: error: passing argument 2 of 'getline'
      from incompatible pointer type [-Wincompatible-pointer-types]

which fails the whole bluez build, and with it any device that sets
BLUETOOTH_SUPPORT="yes". Give bytes_read the type getline() actually writes
through and split the declaration, since position stays an int.
--- a/tools/hciattach_rome.c
+++ b/tools/hciattach_rome.c
@@ -829,7 +829,8 @@
 	char *line = NULL;
 	char *pch = NULL;
 	char param_str[20];
-	int bytes_read = 0, position;
+	size_t bytes_read = 0;
+	int position;
 	int ret = -1;
 
 	if (!file_path || !param) {
